 "Halliggye Fogou has a long narrow tunnel [S2]; it is roofed and walled in stone [S3]; the tunnel leads to three chambers [S2]; it is the largest and best-preserved of several tunnels linked to Cornish Iron Age settlements [S3]; those tunnels are mysterious [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-pilot-2026-09-26c: verifier teaser-verify-002 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-pilot-2026-09-26c/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Halliggye Fogou is a fogou, an underground stone tunnel complex, in Cornwall, England [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halliggye_Fogou]; It consists of a long narrow tunnel [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halliggye_Fogou]; The tunnel is roofed and walled in stone [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/halliggye-fogou/]; The tunnel leads to three chambers [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halliggye_Fogou]; It is the largest and best-preserved of several such tunnels [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/halliggye-fogou/]; These tunnels are mysterious (their purpose is unknown) [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/halliggye-fogou/]; These tunnels are linked to Cornish Iron Age settlements [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/halliggye-fogou/]"}]'::jsonb),
